"[PDF] Prevent page unloading in PDFiumPage::GenerateThumbnail()" (crbugs
579818899 and 581211065, not public; no CVE listed yet): a PDF's JavaScript
could unload the page while GenerateThumbnail() was rendering it. chromium/src
main commit df0e8fe2c59b03d95759c13e330ccd08d3951643 (main@{#1733082}),
merged on 2026-11-03 to the 157 branch
(b14bfbee941676b34bbb5515e20dd8c95bc22196, refs/branch-heads/8103@{#1093},
after the 157.0.8103.44 tag), and to the 156 and 158 branches. Drop it once
a 157 tag has it.

diff --git a/pdf/pdfium/pdfium_page.cc b/pdf/pdfium/pdfium_page.cc
index 20d3fb1d7..c240343 100644
--- a/pdf/pdfium/pdfium_page.cc
+++ b/pdf/pdfium/pdfium_page.cc
@@ -2148,6 +2148,9 @@
   DCHECK(available());
 
   FPDF_PAGE page = GetPage();
+  // Make sure `page` stays valid for the duration of this function.
+  ScopedPageUnloadPreventer scoped_unload_preventer(this);
+
   const bool has_alpha = !!FPDFPage_HasTransparency(page);
   const int format = has_alpha ? FPDFBitmap_BGRA : FPDFBitmap_BGRx;
 
